asi-complete separation was detected", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["separation"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 93, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[106, 112]], "note": "Divider, Section 4 heading, Sensitivity Analysis 1 subheading"}, {"id": 94, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[113, 113]], "assertion": "height, weight, and yellow cards were added as player-level covariates in sensitivity analysis 1", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["height", "weight", "yellow cards"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 95, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[114, 114]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 96, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[115, 115]], "assertion": "with extended adjustment, RD=0.270pp, OR=1.23, p=0.032", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference", "odds ratio"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 97, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[116, 116]], "assertion": "the effect was essentially unchanged (-0.006pp) with extended adjustment, suggesting robustness to additional confounding", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 98, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[117, 119]], "note": "blank, Sensitivity Analysis 2 subheading, blank"}, {"id": 99, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[120, 121]], "note": "table header and divider row"}, {"id": 100, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[122, 122]], "assertion": "in Germany, N=33,689 dyads (31,916 light/1,773 dark), RD=1.22pp, OR=2.59, p<0.001", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["Germany"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 101, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[123, 123]], "assertion": "in England, N=24,727 dyads (20,851 light/3,876 dark), RD=0.35pp, OR=1.33, p=0.075", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["England"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 102, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[124, 124]], "assertion": "in Spain, N=22,802 dyads (21,535 light/1,267 dark), RD=0.04pp, OR=1.03, p=0.911", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["Spain"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 103, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[125, 125]], "assertion": "in France, N=11,833 dyads (9,353 light/2,480 dark), RD=-0.30pp, OR=0.83, p=0.324", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["France"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 104, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[126, 126]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 105, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[127, 127]], "assertion": "there is extremely strong heterogeneity in the effect across leagues", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["league heterogeneity"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [106, 107]}, {"id": 106, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[127, 127]], "assertion": "the overall significant result is driven almost entirely by Germany", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["Germany"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [105, 107]}, {"id": 107, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[127, 127]], "assertion": "England shows a marginal effect while Spain shows no effect and France shows a non-significant reversal", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["England", "Spain", "France"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [105, 106]}, {"id": 108, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[128, 130]], "note": "blank, Sensitivity Analysis 3 subheading, blank"}, {"id": 109, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[131, 131]], "assertion": "sensitivity analysis 3 was restricted to skin tone 0.0 vs 1.0 only (N=38,359 dyads)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["skin tone extremes"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 110, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[132, 132]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 111, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[133, 133]], "assertion": "the extreme comparison yielded RD=0.35pp, OR=1.33, p=0.022", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference", "odds ratio"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 112, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[134, 134]], "assertion": "the effect is slightly larger at the extremes, consistent with a dose-response relationship between darkness and bias", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["dose-response"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 113, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[135, 141]], "note": "Divider, Section 5 heading, and 'Formal Statistical Conclusion' subheading"}, {"id": 114, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[142, 142]], "assertion": "the formal statistical conclusion is that the hypothesis is SUPPORTED", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 115, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[143, 143]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 116, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[144, 144]], "note": "restates the conclusion as a lead-in to the supporting bullet list"}, {"id": 117, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[145, 145]], "assertion": "the primary estimand (RD) is 0.28pp with 95% CI excluding zero (0.03-0.56), p=0.028<0.05", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 118, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[146, 146]], "assertion": "the secondary estimand (OR) is 1.24 with 95% CI excluding one (1.02-1.50)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["odds ratio"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 119, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[147, 147]], "assertion": "the effect direction is consistent with the hypothesis", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect direction"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 120, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[148, 148]], "assertion": "the effect persists after adjustment for position, league, and exposure", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["adjusted effect"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 121, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[149, 151]], "note": "blank, 'Critical Evaluation and Caveats' subheading, blank"}, {"id": 122, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[152, 152]], "note": "lead-in stating the conclusion must be heavily qualified"}, {"id": 123, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[153, 155]], "note": "blank, 'Major Limitations:' label, blank"}, {"id": 124, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[156, 156]], "assertion": "the absolute effect size (0.28 percentage points) is very small", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 125, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[157, 157]], "assertion": "baseline risk moving from 1.21% to 1.49% is a modest absolute increase", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["baseline risk"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 126, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[158, 158]], "assertion": "approximately 362 dyads are needed to observe one additional red card", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["number needed to expose"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 127, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[159, 159]], "assertion": "the effect is much smaller than league effects (France vs England ~1.2pp difference)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["league effects"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 128, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[160, 160]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 129, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[161, 161]], "assertion": "the statistical significance is borderline", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["statistical significance"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 130, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[162, 162]], "assertion": "the p-value of 0.028 is just barely below α=0.05", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["p-value"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 131, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[163, 163]], "assertion": "the confidence interval just barely excludes zero (lower bound=0.027)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confidence interval"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 132, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[164, 164]], "assertion": "no adjustment for multiple comparisons was made despite conducting subgroup analyses", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["multiple comparisons"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 133, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[165, 165]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 134, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[166, 166]], "assertion": "there is extreme heterogeneity across leagues", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["league heterogeneity"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 135, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[167, 167]], "assertion": "Germany shows a large effect (OR=2.59, p<0.001)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["Germany"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 136, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[168, 168]], "assertion": "England shows a marginal effect (OR=1.33, p=0.075)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["England"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 137, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[169, 169]], "assertion": "Spain shows no effect (OR=1.03, p=0.91)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["Spain"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 138, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[170, 170]], "assertion": "France shows a protective but non-significant effect (OR=0.83, p=0.32)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["France"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 139, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[171, 171]], "assertion": "the overall result is driven primarily by Germany", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["Germany"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 140, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[172, 172]], "note": "raises questions about generalizability and alternative explanations, no specific action named"}, {"id": 141, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[173, 173]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 142, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[174, 174]], "note": "'Potential residual confounding' item label"}, {"id": 143, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[175, 175]], "assertion": "adjustment for position may not fully capture playing style or aggression", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["position adjustment"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 144, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[176, 176]], "assertion": "no data on fouls committed, disciplinary history, or gameplay context was available", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["fouls", "disciplinary history"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 145, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[177, 177]], "assertion": "skin tone's association with country of origin was not controlled for", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["country of origin"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 146, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[178, 178]], "note": "cannot rule out unmeasured confounders, general caveat with no specific action named"}, {"id": 147, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[179, 179]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 148, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[180, 180]], "note": "'Statistical model limitations' item label"}, {"id": 149, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[181, 181]], "assertion": "no clustering adjustment was made even though dyads are nested within players and referees", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["clustering"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 150, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[182, 182]], "assertion": "standard errors are likely underestimated, yielding conservative p-values", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["standard errors"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 151, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[183, 183]], "note": "may lead to overstated precision, general caveat"}, {"id": 152, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[184, 184]], "assertion": "proper multi-way clustering would likely have increased the uncertainty estimates", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["clustering"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 153, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[185, 185]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 154, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[186, 186]], "note": "'Measurement concerns' item label"}, {"id": 155, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[187, 187]], "assertion": "lighting was not standardized across the photos used for skin tone rating", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["photo lighting"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 156, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[188, 188]], "assertion": "medium skin tones (31% of the data) were excluded", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["medium skin tone"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 157, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[189, 189]], "note": "may misclassify multiracial or tanned players, general caveat"}, {"id": 158, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[190, 190]], "assertion": "the binary exposure oversimplifies a continuous skin-tone construct", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["binary exposure"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 159, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[191, 191]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 160, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[192, 192]], "note": "'Data structure and interpretation' item label"}, {"id": 161, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[193, 193]], "assertion": "the unit is the dyad rather than individual games, aggregating across multiple encounters", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["unit of analysis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 162, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[194, 194]], "assertion": "within-game dynamics or specific contexts cannot be assessed due to dyad-level aggregation", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["within-game dynamics"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 163, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[195, 195]], "assertion": "red cards are rare events (1.23% rate), limiting statistical power", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["red card rate"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 164, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[196, 196]], "assertion": "the design is unbalanced (90% light skin, 10% dark skin)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sample balance"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 165, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[197, 199]], "note": "blank, 'Strengths:' label, blank"}, {"id": 166, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[200, 200]], "assertion": "the sample size is large (93,051 dyads, 1,129 players)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sample size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 167, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[201, 201]], "assertion": "the outcome (red card) is objective and documented", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["outcome"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 168, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[202, 202]], "assertion": "blind raters achieved high inter-rater reliability (r=0.92)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["rater reliability"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 169, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[203, 203]], "assertion": "the model adjusted for key confounders (position, league, exposure)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["position", "league", "exposure"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 170, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[204, 204]], "assertion": "results were robust to extended adjustment (height, weight, yellow cards)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["extended adjustment"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 171, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[205, 205]], "assertion": "the effect is larger at the extremes (very light vs very dark), suggesting dose-response", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["dose-response"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 172, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[206, 208]], "note": "blank, 'Substantive Interpretation' subheading, blank"}, {"id": 173, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[209, 209]], "assertion": "taken at face value, the adjusted estimate suggests a small but statistically detectable association between darker skin tone and red card probability", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["adjusted estimate"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 174, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[209, 209]], "note": "lead-in to the list of factors undermining a causal interpretation"}, {"id": 175, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[210, 210]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 176, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[211, 211]], "note": "'Alternative explanations remain plausible:' label"}, {"id": 177, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[212, 212]], "assertion": "cultural or national-origin confounding is a plausible alternative explanation since skin tone correlates with country", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["country of origin"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 178, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[213, 213]], "assertion": "unmeasured playing-style differences (aggression, fouling rates) are a plausible confounder", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["playing style"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 179, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[214, 214]], "assertion": "league-specific factors in Germany may be driving the result", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["Germany"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 180, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[215, 215]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 181, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[216, 216]], "assertion": "the effect is not consistent across contexts, given massive heterogeneity by league", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["league heterogeneity"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 182, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[217, 217]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 183, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[218, 218]], "assertion": "the absolute magnitude of the effect is extremely small and may not be practically meaningful", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 184, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[219, 219]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 185, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[220, 220]], "assertion": "the statistical evidence is weak, given the borderline p-value and fragile CI", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["statistical evidence"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 186, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[221, 223]], "note": "blank, 'Recommendation' subheading, blank"}, {"id": 187, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[224, 224]], "assertion": "the analysis formally supports the hypothesis by conventional statistical criteria (p<0.05, CI excludes 0)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [188, 189, 190]}, {"id": 188, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[224, 224]], "assertion": "the author remains highly skeptical that this represents meaningful evidence of referee bias", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["referee bias"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [187, 189, 190]}, {"id": 189, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[224, 224]], "assertion": "the small effect size, borderline significance, heterogeneity, and potential confounding together suggest caution in interpretation", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["overall evidence"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [187, 188, 190]}, {"id": 190, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[224, 224]], "assertion": "the result appears driven primarily by Germany, raising the question of a general phenomenon versus a country-specific artifact", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["Germany"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [187, 188, 189]}, {"id": 191, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[225, 225]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 192, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[226, 226]], "assertion": "a more appropriate conclusion would frame the evidence as weak, inconsistent across leagues, and of questionable practical significance rather than as SUPPORTED", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["conclusion wording"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [193]}, {"id": 193, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[226, 226]], "assertion": "further research using game-level data controlling for foul rates and playing style would be needed to assess genuine referee bias, but was not conducted here", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["future research"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [192]}, {"id": 194, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[227, 233]], "note": "Divider, Section 6 heading, and 'Confounding and Selection Bias' subheading"}, {"id": 195, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[234, 234]], "assertion": "the analysis cannot control for playing style, aggression, foul rates, disciplinary history, or country of origin", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["unmeasured confounders"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 196, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[235, 235]], "assertion": "14.7% of players are missing photos (and thus skin tone data), and this missingness is potentially non-random", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["missing data"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 197, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[236, 236]], "assertion": "conditioning on position may induce collider bias if position mediates the skin tone to red card relationship", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["position", "collider bias"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 198, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[237, 239]], "note": "blank, 'Measurement Error' subheading, blank"}, {"id": 199, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[240, 240]], "assertion": "skin tone ratings came from non-standardized photos with varying lighting, photo quality, and angle", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["photo standardization"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 200, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[241, 241]], "assertion": "dichotomizing the continuous skin tone scale loses information and may misclassify borderline cases", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["binary exposure"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 201, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[242, 242]], "assertion": "the binary 'any red card' outcome collapses counts, treating 1 and 2 red cards equally", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["outcome variable"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 202, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[243, 245]], "note": "blank, 'Statistical Modeling Assumptions' subheading, blank"}, {"id": 203, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[246, 246]], "assertion": "no clustering adjustment was made even though observations are not independent, likely underestimating standard errors", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["clustering"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 204, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[247, 247]], "assertion": "a linear relationship between number of games and log-odds of red card was assumed", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["games"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 205, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[248, 248]], "assertion": "no interactions were tested even though the effect may vary by position or league", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["interactions"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 206, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[249, 249]], "assertion": "the 1.23% red card rate may challenge the asymptotic assumptions underlying the logistic regression", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["rare event"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 207, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[250, 252]], "note": "blank, 'Generalizability' subheading, blank"}, {"id": 208, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[253, 253]], "assertion": "the data used are only from the 2012-2013 season", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["data time period"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 209, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[253, 253]], "note": "trends may have changed since then, general caveat"}, {"id": 210, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[254, 254]], "assertion": "the data cover only four European leagues", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["geographic scope"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 211, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[254, 254]], "note": "may not generalize to other regions, general caveat"}, {"id": 212, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[255, 255]], "assertion": "the study includes male players only, so results cannot generalize to women's soccer", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["player sex"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 213, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[256, 256]], "assertion": "the data are restricted to the professional level", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["professional level"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 214, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[256, 256]], "note": "may not apply to amateur or youth leagues, general caveat"}, {"id": 215, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[257, 259]], "note": "blank, 'Causal Inference Limitations' subheading, blank"}, {"id": 216, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[260, 260]], "assertion": "the observational design cannot rule out reverse causation or unmeasured confounding", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["study design"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 217, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[261, 261]], "assertion": "no randomization was used, so a causal effect of skin tone on referee decisions cannot be claimed", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["randomization"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 218, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[262, 262]], "assertion": "league-level implicit bias measures were not used in the primary model", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["implicit bias measures"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 219, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[263, 267]], "note": "Divider, Section 7 heading, blank"}, {"id": 220, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[268, 268]], "assertion": "all data were successfully loaded and analyzed", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["data loading"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [221, 222]}, {"id": 221, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[268, 268]], "assertion": "no evidence of data corruption or severe quality issues was found", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["data quality"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [220, 222]}, {"id": 222, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[268, 268]], "assertion": "missing data was handled via complete-case analysis (listwise deletion)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["missing data"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [220, 221]}, {"id": 223, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[268, 268]], "note": "assumes data are MCAR, an untestable assumption that may not hold"}, {"id": 224, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[269, 269]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 225, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[270, 270]], "assertion": "variables matched the codebook description, with skin tone on the expected 0-1 scale and red cards ranging 0-2", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["codebook alignment"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 226, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[271, 275]], "note": "Divider, Section 8 heading, blank"}, {"id": 227, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[276, 276]], "assertion": "the random seed was set to 42 for the parametric bootstrap", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["random seed"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [228, 229, 230]}, {"id": 228, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[276, 276]], "assertion": "specific software versions were used (Python 3.x, pandas, numpy, scipy, statsmodels, matplotlib, seaborn)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["software versions"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [227, 229, 230]}, {"id": 229, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[276, 276]], "assertion": "the analysis was conducted on 2025-11-12", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["analysis date"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [227, 228, 230]}, {"id": 230, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[276, 276]], "assertion": "all analyses are fully reproducible using the submitted Python script (final_analysis.py)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["reproducibility"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [227, 228, 229]}, {"id": 231, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[277, 277]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 232, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[278, 278]], "note": "'End of Report' marker"}]}}